<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Gajapati Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1434 CE – 1541 CE · capital Cuttack</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Suryavamsi kingdom of Odisha whose Gajapati kings, devotees of Jagannath at Puri, briefly ruled from the Ganges to the Kaveri.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1434 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapilendra-deva">Kapilendra Deva</a>, a minister and general of the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-ganga-dynasty">Eastern Ganga</a> king, seized the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a> and founded the Suryavamsi dynasty. He took the title Gajapati, lord of elephants, and launched campaigns that pushed the kingdom's frontiers south along the eastern coast and north into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapilendra-deva">Kapilendra Deva</a> conquered coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-region">Andhra</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/reddi-kingdom">Reddi Kingdom</a> and raided as far as the Kaveri, defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>. The kings ruled as servants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a> of Puri, whose temple was the centre of state ritual. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prataparudra-deva">Prataparudra Deva</a> hosted the saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaitanya-mahaprabhu">Chaitanya</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odia-language">Odia</a> literature flourished with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarala-das">Sarala Das's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara</a> took the southern provinces from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prataparudra-deva">Prataparudra</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/golconda-sultanate">Golconda Sultanate</a> pressed from the south-west. In 1541 the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govinda-vidyadhara">Govinda Vidyadhara</a> killed the last Suryavamsi heirs and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhoi-dynasty">Bhoi dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gajapati-kingdom.jpg" alt="Gajapati Kingdom" width="320" height="296"><figcaption>Image: Ashok3932 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Gajapatis_(1).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1434 CE – 1541 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cuttack</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kapilendra Deva, Purushottama Deva, Prataparudra Deva</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism (Jagannath cult)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia, Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Suryavamsi Gajapatis, Gajapati Empire, Gajapatis of Odisha</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1488&amp;focus=gajapati-kingdom" aria-label="Gajapati Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6990 1418 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gajapati Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7310 1674L7181 1846M7310 1674L7313 1677M7310 1674L7313 1677"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7181 1846h0M7313 1677h0M7313 1677h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7310 1674h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7310 1674h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1488&amp;focus=gajapati-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
